      "verified": true,
      "fine_trace_step": 1,
      "description": "Source. During `global_read()`'s type-discovery scan, `scn_dwarf_type()` resolves the attacker-controlled section-name offset through the attacker-controlled shstrtab and materializes section 2's misleading name as `.debug_line_str`, which is the earliest project-side state that puts this non-string `SHT_GNU_HASH` section on the vulnerable DWARF path."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "r_gnuhash_output_fully_initialized_before_publish",
      "role": "root_cause",
      "file": "libelf/gnuhash_xlate.h",
      "function": "elf_cvt_gnuhash",
      "line": 69,
      "operands": [
        "len",
        "initialized prefix of dest[0..len)"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "le",
        "left": "len",
        "right": "initialized prefix of dest[0..len)"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_gnuhash_output_fully_initialized_before_tail_scan",
      "fine_trace_step": 13,
      "description": "Root cause. The vulnerable GNU-hash converter only writes complete 4-byte units after the control-word phase and has no fallback copy for leftover bytes. For the exact 158-byte witness, the earlier control words set `bitmask_words = 0`, this loop consumes 35 full words, and the final two bytes of the destination buffer remain uninitialized."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "n_string_tail_scan_reads_past_initialized_prefix",
      "role": "sink",
      "file": "libdw/dwarf_begin_elf.c",
      "function": "check_section",
      "line": 265,
      "operands": [
        "initialized prefix of ((const char *) data->d_buf)[0..size)",
        "size"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "lt",
        "left": "initialized prefix of ((const char *) data->d_buf)[0..size)",
        "right": "size"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_string_tail_scan_reads_past_initialized_prefix",
      "fine_trace_step": 16,
      "description": "MSAN sink. Because `.debug_line_str` is treated as a string section, this backward trim loop reads `data->d_buf[size - 1]`; on the saved witness the first iteration dereferences `data->d_buf[157]` from the two-byte tail that `elf_cvt_gnuhash()` never wrote."
    },
    {
